2026-09-27T09:10:27.1129851Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1130151Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1130345Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1130597Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1131168Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1131489Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1131653Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1132073Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1132345Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1132546Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1133091Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1133619Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1134693Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1135623Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1135982Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1136807Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1137708Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1138179Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1138686Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1139387Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1139521Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1139828Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1140005Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1224810Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1231203Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1231626Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1232373Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1233534Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1234458Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1235315Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1236272Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1236906Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1237062Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1237416Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1237626Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1239325Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1241188Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1242226Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1243628Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:27.1243956Z 
